{"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/sarraverse/gpi-gridworld-multiseed?scriptVersionId=365281433\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e16a1afb","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002483,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.726623+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.72414+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["# Generalized Policy Iteration in a Tiny GridWorld\n","\n","**A reproducible illustration of how policy evaluation and policy improvement can interact at different update frequencies.**\n","\n","This notebook compares two tabular Q-learning schedules in the same deterministic 5×5 GridWorld:\n","\n","1. **Interleaved updates:** update the action-value function after every transition. The behavior policy can respond to the latest estimates on the next action.\n","2. **Alternating batches:** collect a batch of episodes using a fixed ε-greedy behavior policy based on the current greedy policy, then update the action-value function from the collected transitions before constructing the next batch's policy.\n","\n","Both schedules combine value estimation and policy improvement. This is **not** a comparison of GPI against a non-GPI method. It is a small experiment about the granularity at which learning updates and policy changes interact.\n","\n","We repeat the comparison across multiple random seeds and report mean ± standard deviation. The environment and hyperparameters are intentionally small so the notebook runs on a CPU.\n","\n","> **Interpretation caution:** Q-learning is an off-policy control algorithm. Its update target uses the maximum estimated next-state action value. The experiment uses Q-learning as a convenient value-based example; it does not implement a textbook policy-evaluation procedure such as iterative policy evaluation for a fixed policy.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"7bbe0fb5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.001738,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.730436+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.728698+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 1. Imports and experiment configuration\n","\n","No GPU or deep-learning framework is required. The main experiment uses NumPy and Matplotlib.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":1,"id":"e3f8a374","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.735625Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.735073Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.746397Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.745705Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.015677,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.747971+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.732294+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Seeds: 10\n","Training episodes per seed and method: 500\n","Total training episodes per method: 5,000\n"]}],"source":["import numpy as np\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","from collections import defaultdict\n","from dataclasses import dataclass\n","\n","# Environment\n","GRID_SIZE = 5\n","START = (0, 0)\n","GOAL = (4, 4)\n","WALLS = {(1, 1), (1, 2), (3, 2)}\n","\n","# Actions: up, down, left, right\n","ACTIONS = {\n","    0: (-1, 0),\n","    1: (1, 0),\n","    2: (0, -1),\n","    3: (0, 1),\n","}\n","ACTION_NAMES = [\"↑\", \"↓\", \"←\", \"→\"]\n","\n","STEP_REWARD = -1.0\n","GOAL_REWARD = 10.0\n","MAX_STEPS = 50\n","\n","# Learning\n","ALPHA = 0.20\n","GAMMA = 0.95\n","EPSILON = 0.10\n","\n","# Experiment\n","N_EPISODES = 500\n","BATCH_SIZE = 10\n","EVAL_INTERVAL = 50\n","EVAL_EPISODES = 100\n","SEEDS = list(range(10))\n","\n","print(f\"Seeds: {len(SEEDS)}\")\n","print(f\"Training episodes per seed and method: {N_EPISODES}\")\n","print(f\"Total training episodes per method: {N_EPISODES * len(SEEDS):,}\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"77042dd6","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.001809,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.751677+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.749868+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 2. Define the GridWorld\n","\n","The agent starts at `S` and aims to reach `G`. Gray cells are blocked. Each move costs −1, and reaching the goal gives +10. An episode ends when the agent reaches the goal or hits the 50-step limit.\n","\n","The shortest route in this map requires eight moves, so a successful shortest-path episode receives a return of +3.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":2,"id":"6987bc7e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.75653Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.756242Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.924262Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.923574Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.172387,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.925874+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.753487+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 500x500 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["def step(state, action):\n","    \"\"\"Apply one action; return (next_state, reward, done).\"\"\"\n","    dr, dc = ACTIONS[action]\n","    candidate = (state[0] + dr, state[1] + dc)\n","\n","    inside_grid = (\n","        0 <= candidate[0] < GRID_SIZE\n","        and 0 <= candidate[1] < GRID_SIZE\n","    )\n","    if not inside_grid or candidate in WALLS:\n","        candidate = state\n","\n","    done = candidate == GOAL\n","    reward = GOAL_REWARD if done else STEP_REWARD\n","    return candidate, reward, done\n","\n","\n","def draw_grid():\n","    grid = np.zeros((GRID_SIZE, GRID_SIZE))\n","    for row, col in WALLS:\n","        grid[row, col] = 1\n","\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5, 5))\n","    ax.imshow(grid, cmap=\"Greys\", vmin=0, vmax=1)\n","    ax.set_xticks(np.arange(-0.5, GRID_SIZE, 1), minor=True)\n","    ax.set_yticks(np.arange(-0.5, GRID_SIZE, 1), minor=True)\n","    ax.grid(which=\"minor\", color=\"black\", linewidth=1)\n","    ax.set_xticks([])\n","    ax.set_yticks([])\n","    ax.text(START[1], START[0], \"S\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n","            fontsize=16, fontweight=\"bold\")\n","    ax.text(GOAL[1], GOAL[0], \"G\", ha=\"center\", va=\"center\",\n","            fontsize=16, fontweight=\"bold\")\n","    ax.set_title(\"5×5 GridWorld\")\n","    plt.show()\n","\n","\n","draw_grid()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"24d94255","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002115,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.930246+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.928131+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 3. Q-learning utilities\n","\n","The one-step Q-learning update is:\n","\n","\\[\n","Q(s,a) \\leftarrow Q(s,a) + \\alpha\n","\\left[r + \\gamma\\max_{a'} Q(s',a') - Q(s,a)\\right],\n","\\]\n","\n","with the terminal-state target set to the immediate reward.\n","\n","The ε-greedy behavior policy explores with probability ε and otherwise chooses an action with the highest current Q-value. Ties are broken randomly during training to avoid a systematic directional bias.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":3,"id":"ea9b6b79","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.93581Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.935541Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.944658Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.944034Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.013933,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.946221+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.932288+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def epsilon_greedy_action(q, state, rng, epsilon=EPSILON):\n","    \"\"\"Choose an epsilon-greedy action, randomizing among greedy ties.\"\"\"\n","    if rng.random() < epsilon:\n","        return int(rng.integers(len(ACTIONS)))\n","\n","    values = np.array([q[(state, action)] for action in ACTIONS])\n","    best_actions = np.flatnonzero(np.isclose(values, values.max()))\n","    return int(rng.choice(best_actions))\n","\n","\n","def q_update(q, state, action, reward, next_state, done):\n","    \"\"\"Perform one tabular Q-learning update.\"\"\"\n","    if done:\n","        target = reward\n","    else:\n","        target = reward + GAMMA * max(\n","            q[(next_state, next_action)] for next_action in ACTIONS\n","        )\n","\n","    q[(state, action)] += ALPHA * (\n","        target - q[(state, action)]\n","    )\n","\n","\n","def greedy_policy(q):\n","    \"\"\"Extract a deterministic greedy policy; ties use the first action.\"\"\"\n","    policy = {}\n","\n","    for row in range(GRID_SIZE):\n","        for col in range(GRID_SIZE):\n","            state = (row, col)\n","\n","            if state == GOAL or state in WALLS:\n","                continue\n","\n","            values = [q[(state, action)] for action in ACTIONS]\n","            policy[state] = int(np.argmax(values))\n","\n","    return policy\n","\n","\n","def run_episode(q, rng, learn_online=True, fixed_policy=None):\n","    \"\"\"Run one episode and return its reward, length, and transitions.\n","\n","    If fixed_policy is supplied, its greedy actions remain fixed for the\n","    episode. Epsilon exploration is still allowed. This supports the\n","    alternating-batch schedule.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    state = START\n","    total_reward = 0.0\n","    transitions = []\n","\n","    for step_index in range(1, MAX_STEPS + 1):\n","        if fixed_policy is None:\n","            action = epsilon_greedy_action(q, state, rng)\n","        elif rng.random() < EPSILON:\n","            action = int(rng.integers(len(ACTIONS)))\n","        else:\n","            action = fixed_policy.get(state, 0)\n","\n","        next_state, reward, done = step(state, action)\n","        transitions.append(\n","            (state, action, reward, next_state, done)\n","        )\n","\n","        if learn_online:\n","            q_update(q, state, action, reward, next_state, done)\n","\n","        total_reward += reward\n","        state = next_state\n","\n","        if done:\n","            break\n","\n","    return total_reward, len(transitions), transitions\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2ff1fd9c","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.001869,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.950495+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.948626+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 4. Greedy-policy evaluation\n","\n","Evaluation is performed without exploration: the agent follows the greedy policy derived from the current Q-table. We report:\n","\n","- **Success rate:** fraction of evaluation episodes that reach the goal.\n","- **Mean episode length:** average number of moves before reaching the goal or hitting the step limit.\n","- **Mean return:** average cumulative reward.\n","\n","We evaluate both methods at the same training checkpoints (every 50 episodes), so their x-axes are directly comparable.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":4,"id":"b79c83df","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.955404Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.955189Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.961054Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.960477Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.010142,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.962565+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.952423+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def evaluate_greedy_policy(q, episodes=EVAL_EPISODES):\n","    \"\"\"Evaluate the current greedy policy without exploration.\"\"\"\n","    policy = greedy_policy(q)\n","    rewards = []\n","    lengths = []\n","    successes = []\n","\n","    for _ in range(episodes):\n","        state = START\n","        total_reward = 0.0\n","        done = False\n","        length = 0\n","\n","        while length < MAX_STEPS and not done:\n","            action = policy.get(state, 0)\n","            state, reward, done = step(state, action)\n","            total_reward += reward\n","            length += 1\n","\n","        rewards.append(total_reward)\n","        lengths.append(length)\n","        successes.append(float(done))\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"mean_reward\": float(np.mean(rewards)),\n","        \"mean_length\": float(np.mean(lengths)),\n","        \"success_rate\": float(np.mean(successes)),\n","    }\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"3209dcbc","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.001846,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.966444+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.964598+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 5. The two training schedules\n","\n","**Interleaved:** the agent updates Q immediately after each transition. Its next action can therefore use the latest estimates.\n","\n","**Alternating batches:** the agent constructs a greedy policy at the beginning of each batch. It collects `BATCH_SIZE` episodes using that fixed greedy policy plus ε exploration. After collecting the batch, it shuffles the transitions and applies Q-learning updates. The next batch uses a newly extracted greedy policy.\n","\n","This is a deliberately simple comparison of update schedules. The alternating method's policy is held fixed within a batch, while exploration remains enabled.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":5,"id":"b17b4621","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.971657Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.971216Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.979615Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.978845Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.012721,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.981214+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.968493+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["def train_interleaved(seed):\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n","    q = defaultdict(float)\n","\n","    train_rewards = []\n","    train_lengths = []\n","    checkpoints = []\n","    eval_metrics = []\n","\n","    for episode in range(1, N_EPISODES + 1):\n","        reward, length, _ = run_episode(\n","            q, rng, learn_online=True\n","        )\n","        train_rewards.append(reward)\n","        train_lengths.append(length)\n","\n","        if episode % EVAL_INTERVAL == 0:\n","            checkpoints.append(episode)\n","            eval_metrics.append(evaluate_greedy_policy(q))\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"q\": q,\n","        \"train_rewards\": np.asarray(train_rewards),\n","        \"train_lengths\": np.asarray(train_lengths),\n","        \"checkpoints\": np.asarray(checkpoints),\n","        \"evaluation\": eval_metrics,\n","        \"final\": evaluate_greedy_policy(q, episodes=EVAL_EPISODES),\n","    }\n","\n","\n","def train_alternating(seed):\n","    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n","    q = defaultdict(float)\n","\n","    train_rewards = []\n","    train_lengths = []\n","    checkpoints = []\n","    eval_metrics = []\n","\n","    completed = 0\n","    while completed < N_EPISODES:\n","        # Freeze the current greedy policy for this collection batch.\n","        policy_for_batch = greedy_policy(q)\n","        batch_transitions = []\n","\n","        batch_episodes = min(\n","            BATCH_SIZE, N_EPISODES - completed\n","        )\n","\n","        for _ in range(batch_episodes):\n","            reward, length, transitions = run_episode(\n","                q,\n","                rng,\n","                learn_online=False,\n","                fixed_policy=policy_for_batch,\n","            )\n","            train_rewards.append(reward)\n","            train_lengths.append(length)\n","            batch_transitions.extend(transitions)\n","            completed += 1\n","\n","        # Apply learning updates after the batch has been collected.\n","        rng.shuffle(batch_transitions)\n","        for transition in batch_transitions:\n","            q_update(q, *transition)\n","\n","        if completed % EVAL_INTERVAL == 0:\n","            checkpoints.append(completed)\n","            eval_metrics.append(evaluate_greedy_policy(q))\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"q\": q,\n","        \"train_rewards\": np.asarray(train_rewards),\n","        \"train_lengths\": np.asarray(train_lengths),\n","        \"checkpoints\": np.asarray(checkpoints),\n","        \"evaluation\": eval_metrics,\n","        \"final\": evaluate_greedy_policy(q, episodes=EVAL_EPISODES),\n","    }\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"be6b6697","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002422,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.985643+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.983221+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 6. Run the multi-seed experiment\n","\n","Each method is trained independently for every seed. We use the same list of seed values for both methods, though the two methods consume random numbers differently because their interaction schedules differ.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":6,"id":"e42ad911","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.990296Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.990108Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.081783Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.08082Z"},"papermill":{"duration":3.096072,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.083603+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:07.987531+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Run 1/10 — seed 0\n","Run 2/10 — seed 1\n","Run 3/10 — seed 2\n","Run 4/10 — seed 3\n","Run 5/10 — seed 4\n","Run 6/10 — seed 5\n","Run 7/10 — seed 6\n","Run 8/10 — seed 7\n","Run 9/10 — seed 8\n","Run 10/10 — seed 9\n","\\nAll runs completed.\n"]}],"source":["interleaved_runs = []\n","alternating_runs = []\n","\n","for run_number, seed in enumerate(SEEDS, start=1):\n","    print(f\"Run {run_number}/{len(SEEDS)} — seed {seed}\")\n","\n","    interleaved_runs.append(train_interleaved(seed))\n","    alternating_runs.append(train_alternating(seed))\n","\n","print(\"\\\\nAll runs completed.\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"9e147ce0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002597,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.089024+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.086427+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 7. Aggregate results across seeds\n","\n","We report the mean and standard deviation across independent runs. These are descriptive statistics for this small experiment, not a formal statistical test.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":7,"id":"19e6b333","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.095481Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.095088Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.106347Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.105566Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.016623,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.108151+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.091528+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Interleaved: reward=3.00 ± 0.00, steps=8.00 ± 0.00, success=100.0% ± 0.0%\n","Alternating batches: reward=3.00 ± 0.00, steps=8.00 ± 0.00, success=100.0% ± 0.0%\n"]}],"source":["def aggregate_evaluations(runs, metric):\n","    values = np.array([\n","        [point[metric] for point in run[\"evaluation\"]]\n","        for run in runs\n","    ])\n","    return values.mean(axis=0), values.std(axis=0)\n","\n","\n","checkpoints = interleaved_runs[0][\"checkpoints\"]\n","\n","# Verify that both schedules were evaluated at the same checkpoints.\n","assert all(np.array_equal(run[\"checkpoints\"], checkpoints)\n","           for run in interleaved_runs)\n","assert all(np.array_equal(run[\"checkpoints\"], checkpoints)\n","           for run in alternating_runs)\n","\n","metrics = [\"success_rate\", \"mean_length\", \"mean_reward\"]\n","aggregated = {}\n","\n","for metric in metrics:\n","    aggregated[(\"interleaved\", metric)] = aggregate_evaluations(\n","        interleaved_runs, metric\n","    )\n","    aggregated[(\"alternating\", metric)] = aggregate_evaluations(\n","        alternating_runs, metric\n","    )\n","\n","def summarize_final(runs, method_name):\n","    final_rewards = np.array([run[\"final\"][\"mean_reward\"] for run in runs])\n","    final_lengths = np.array([run[\"final\"][\"mean_length\"] for run in runs])\n","    final_success = np.array([run[\"final\"][\"success_rate\"] for run in runs])\n","\n","    return {\n","        \"method\": method_name,\n","        \"reward_mean\": final_rewards.mean(),\n","        \"reward_std\": final_rewards.std(),\n","        \"length_mean\": final_lengths.mean(),\n","        \"length_std\": final_lengths.std(),\n","        \"success_mean\": final_success.mean(),\n","        \"success_std\": final_success.std(),\n","    }\n","\n","summary_rows = [\n","    summarize_final(interleaved_runs, \"Interleaved\"),\n","    summarize_final(alternating_runs, \"Alternating batches\"),\n","]\n","\n","for row in summary_rows:\n","    print(\n","        f\"{row['method']}: \"\n","        f\"reward={row['reward_mean']:.2f} ± {row['reward_std']:.2f}, \"\n","        f\"steps={row['length_mean']:.2f} ± {row['length_std']:.2f}, \"\n","        f\"success={row['success_mean']:.1%} ± {row['success_std']:.1%}\"\n","    )\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"e7dc562b","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.002627,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.113338+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.110711+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## 8. Plot evaluation learning curves\n","\n","Shaded regions show ±1 standard deviation across seeds. The success-rate plot is often the easiest to interpret: it shows how reliably the current greedy policy reaches the goal as training progresses.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":8,"id":"200f9d21","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.119869Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.119594Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.644144Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.64332Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.529826,"end_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.645886+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-03T13:05:11.11606+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 800x450 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 800x450 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"},{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 800x450 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["plot_specs = [\n","    (\"success_rate\", \"Greedy evaluation success rate\", \"Success rate\", (0, 1.05)),\n","    (\"mean_length\", \"Greedy evaluation episode length\", \"Steps\", None),\n","    (\"mean_reward\", \"Greedy evaluation mean return\", \"Return\", None),\n","]\n","\n","for metric, title, ylabel, ylim in plot_specs:\n","    online_mean, online_std = aggregated[(\"interleaved\", metric)]\n","    batch_mean, batch_std = aggregated[(\"alternating\", metric)]\n","\n","    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4.5))\n","\n","    ax.plot(checkpoints, online_mean, marker=\"o\", label=\"Interleaved\")\n","    ax.fill_between(\n","        checkpoints,\n","        online_mean - online_std,\n","        online_mean + online_std,\n","        alpha=0.18,\n","    )\n","\n","    ax.plot(checkpoints, batch_mean, marker=\"s\", label=\"Alternating batches\")\n","    ax.fill_between(\n","        checkpoints,\n","        batch_mean - batch_std,\n","        batch_mean + batch_std,\n","        alpha=0.18,\n","    )\n","\n","    ax.set_title(title)\n","    ax.set_xlabel(\"Training episodes\")\n","    ax.set_ylabel(ylabel)\n","    if ylim is not None:\n","        ax.set_ylim(*ylim)\n","    ax.grid(alpha=0.25)\n","